@startuml storage-layout
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
title M-DP3: dispatcher storage ownership and durable ordering, service slices (draft)
component "swarma-dispatcher process\nservice daemon from slice 0\nservice UID swarma-dispatcher" as D
component "Supervisor\ndaemon-owned\nsame service UID" as S
folder "Service-private state root (dispatcher-owned)\n/opt/swarma/services/swarma-dispatcher/state\nmode 0700 (§4.1)" as ROOT {
  artifact "Immutable input/1\ncaller principal + root request_id, canonical request,\nplan bytes, full caller chain, digests,\nlifecycle authorisation + machine-owned network pin (§4.2)" as INPUT
  artifact "agent/1 allocations\nuid + generation, binding / leaf / caller chain IDs,\nregistered caller key, ordinary expiry / standing designation, cleanup (§4.3)" as AG
  artifact "run/1 executions\nowner + input, plan digest, execution claim + epoch,\nordinary-only runtime deadline; supervisor/start/termination evidence, outcome (§§4.4, 6)" as RUN
  artifact "Effect table\nid, component, operation, intent, result, observation (§4.5)" as EFFECT
  artifact "Journal\nappend + flush before external effect; replay at startup" as JOURNAL
  artifact "Index + capacity claims\nowned resources, expires_at (§9)" as CLAIM
  artifact "Host admission permit (SH2+ gated)\nsession-scoped logical_session_id; per-use physical claims/fences; encoding unpublished (§12)" as PERMIT
  artifact "Dispatcher key + lock (§4.1)\nlocal journal/record transitions only; never cross-service waits" as KEY
  artifact "Time watermark + boot-inclusive elapsed evidence\ntrusted advances; explicit reset; encoding unpublished" as TIME
  artifact "Per-record in-flight markers + daemon-instance fence\nintent, immutable arguments, cancel intent; encoding unpublished" as FLIGHT
  artifact "Restore-fence reference / epoch floor / reverse inventory obligations\nmark itself is outside restored domain; encoding unpublished" as RESTORE
  artifact "Bounded private executor output logs (§§6, 13)" as LOG
}
artifact "Operator restore mark\noutside the restored failure domain; location unpublished (§11.1)" as RESTOREMARK
folder "Runtime socket directory from slice 0\n/opt/swarma/run/dispatcher/ (§8.3)" as SOCKET
component "swarma-user-manager (root)\nowns OS account ledger / termination evidence" as H
component "swarma-user-launcher (root until drop)\nwrites start receipt before agent UID exec" as L
component "Credential broker (unprivileged service)\nowns bindings, grants/revocations, leases, credentials" as B
component "curator-run -> harness (agent UID)\nagent-home working directory; own broker connection" as E
D ..> RESTOREMARK : external fence before restored bytes become visible
D --> ROOT : owned state; configuration selects root\nnever inherited HOME
D --> SOCKET : all slices; peer authentication\nno fallback on auth/version/malformed reply
S --> RUN : current daemon-instance epoch required for every write\ndurable registration before launch\nrecord launcher / stop receipts
S --> LOG : bounded output
D --> H : lock intent/in-flight -> unlock call -> lock/fence result
D --> B : unlocked bind/unbind/binding replacement / observations
S --> L : journaled launch intent; immutable plan FD3
L --> E : user-manager §7 descriptor lifecycle (R-FD3)\nroot receipt; UID/GID drop; read-only staged FD3; verified exec
E --> B : own authenticated lease connection
note bottom of ROOT
  Record replacement: temporary file -> flush -> rename -> directory flush.
  Journal replay covers a crash between journal and record replacement (§4.1).
  Input is written once before acceptance; later queue/recovery reads it (§4.2).
  R-LOCK wait graph: state lock -> local journal/record I/O only.
  Unlocked dispatcher workers -> helper/launcher/broker; unlocked host -> dispatcher.
  Per-record waiters release global lock; ownership locks retain separate lifetime.
  Late results revalidate record/daemon/controller fences; no resurrected start/delivery.
  Bounded I/O/concurrency preserves recovery controls during stalled effects.
  Unknown/contradictory evidence keeps records pending: no relaunch,
  no capacity release, no successful cleanup; retry observations (§§4.6, 7.1).
  Standing: no expires_at or lifetime quota; designation encoding unpublished.
  Standing run/1: no runtime deadline or max_runtime quota; ordinary runs keep 4 h / 12 h.
  Sweep never stops standing executions for runtime (§§3.5, 4.4, 7.2).
  Only operator-signed retirement/re-creation (§§4.3, 5.4); never sweep expiry.
  Ordinary: confirmed unbind then local quiesce / declared-key cleanup / home deletion.
  Direct operator retirement retains unconfirmed broker-cleanup obligation.
  Bounded helper deletion batches continue same E-retire; no early UID/quota release.
  Expiry deletion also needs trusted time + monotonic elapsed lifetime.
  E-rebind keeps same random 128-bit generation and old removal tombstone;
  explicit operator retention has no confidentiality guarantee (§5.4); applicable one-shot identity revocation
  is a separate confirmed effect after retirement (§§5.4, 14).
  Subfile names, per-file modes/groups and retention/deletion rules
  are unspecified in spec §§4.1, 6, 13; labels are logical records, not paths.
end note
note right of SOCKET
  Socket basename, owner/group/mode details are unspecified in spec §8.3.
  Broker service UID spelling is unspecified in spec §3.1.
  Control availability after ownership/schema/replay/authentication.
  Forward readiness after complete classification/accounting and confinement.
  Unknown records keep claims; unbounded shared uncertainty closes admission.
  State loss: external restore fence, independent coverage, reverse inventory.
  Orphans await signed operator decision; no automatic/live adoption.
  Maintenance: bounded operator attempt; close admission, inventory, authorized exec.stop,
  confirmed absence/reconciliation before mode/schema/binary change; no live adoption.
  Unknown/refused stop defers change; standing allocations and identities retained.
  Rollback keeps later records and requires compatibility (§11).
end note
note bottom of E
  §5.3 one-shot intake/qualification gate remains closed until published.
  SH2+ target (§12): host service owns metadata/logs/receipts/fences;
  agent runner owns PTY/app-server and renewal. State/log handoff details
  are unspecified in spec §§12, 16; no alternate storage path is asserted.
end note
legend
  Defining spec: [[https://github.com/relux-works/swarma-dispatcher/blob/main/spec/dispatcher.md#41-state-directory §4.1 state directory]]
  [[https://github.com/relux-works/swarma-dispatcher/blob/main/spec/dispatcher.md#83-socket-dispatch1 §8.3 socket]] / §§6, 7.1, 11
endlegend
@enduml
